\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot 4.4.1 Stable\n\n### Issue description\n\n\"scroll_horizontal_enabled\" and \"scroll_vertical_enabled\" properties are ignored for Tree nodes\n\ni expected that setting said properties to false will disable scrolling for the tree, it doesn't, the scrolling gets enabled regardless of the properties values.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. add a tree to a scene\n2. set scrolling_enabled to false for the tree _using the editor inspector_\n3. add enough tree items to trigger scrolling ( or attach the following script )\n```gdscript\nextends Tree\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\t# horizontal scrolling is forcefully enabled for titles\n\tscroll_horizontal_enabled = false\n\tset_column_title(0, \"title \".repeat(100))\n\t\n\t# horizontal scrolling is NOT enabled for items\n\t# but vertical scrolling is forcefully enabled\n\tscroll_vertical_enabled = false\n\tcreate_item().set_text(0, \"root \".repeat(100))\n\tfor i in 100:\n\t\tget_root().create_child().set_text(0, \"child\")\n```\n4. run the scene, you should notice that scrolling is enabled for the tree\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tree_mre.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/20002270/tree_mre.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/u